{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 31, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and a leader of the Crusader state of Tripoli. He was born around 1140 and died in 1187. Raymond was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. *Early Life* Raymond III was a member of the House of Toulouse and was related to several other prominent Crusader leaders. After his father's assassination in 1152 Raymond II's wife Hodierna returned to Jerusalem with her children including Raymond III.\n\nRaymond III became Count of Tripoli in 1152 after the death of his father but as he was still a minor his mother Hodierna acted as regent until 1155. In 1161 Raymond was taken captive by Nur ad-Din Zangi and was held prisoner for nearly ten years. *Imprisonment and Release* During his imprisonment Raymond was forced to ransom himself and was released in 1174. After his release Raymond returned to Tripoli and began to consolidate his power.\n\nUpon his return Raymond III found that his county had been mismanaged during his long absence and he set about restoring order and rebuilding his military. Raymond also became involved in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and played a significant role in the events leading up to the *Battle of Hattin*. Raymond was a skilled military leader and was known for his cautious and pragmatic approach to warfare. He was also a skilled politician and was able to form alliances with other Crusader leaders.\n\nIn 1187 Raymond III played a key role in the events leading up to the Battle of Hattin. He was initially opposed to the idea of attacking Saladin's forces but was eventually persuaded to join the battle. The Crusader army was defeated at Hattin and Raymond III was one of the few leaders to escape. He died soon after the battle possibly due to injuries sustained during the fighting. Raymond III was succeeded by his godson Raymond IV who was the son of Bohemond III of Antioch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.011065074242651463}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0003358753747306764}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.7881377516459906e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0019334923708811402}, {"token": " nob", "logprob": -0.15766973793506622}, {"token": "leman", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.056386951357126236}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.5587414503097534}, {"token": " leader", "logprob": -0.40024620294570923}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0031945884693413973}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Crus", "logprob": -0.9813145995140076}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " state", "logprob": -0.1700276881456375}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.009520012885332108}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.13284537196159363}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.006757384166121483}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.00022015532886143774}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00015805903240107}, {"token": " born", "logprob": -0.030477074906229973}, {"token": " around", "logprob": -0.47408902645111084}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "114", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0003355178632773459}, {"token": " died", "logprob": -0.31531617045402527}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -3.814689989667386e-06}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -4.0531076592742465e-06}, {"token": "118", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "7", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.00016223068814724684}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -0.1384454071521759}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.032154280692338943}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0009188005933538079}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -4.8